{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_008 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) achieved 0.527 acc / 0.510 F1, a clear +4.2% improvement over the RNA-only baseline (config_009, 0.485 acc). This confirms that the pca_n2000 + resnet50 + concat combination is a strong foundation. Uncertainty: We have no evidence yet on whether multiprofile aggregation adds value beyond the single-profile setting. This experiment (config_003) tests exactly that question by switching from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation while holding the RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion (concat) identical to config_008. This is the cleanest possible comparison to isolate the effect of multiprofile + avgpool, changing only the profile/aggregation axis. Under a limited budget, confirming or ruling out the multiprofile benefit on top of the already-validated multimodal pipeline is the highest-information next step before investing in more complex variations (different encoders, transformer aggregation, weighted fusion)."
}

